-- stdin
E.g. this works. I.e. that works too. Use a tibble a.k.a. a data frame. Fit eg. a model or ie. two.

The mean and variance resp. the median are shown. It is approx. 5 cm long. Derive it w.r.t. the mean.

See Fig. 6 and Figs. 7 and 8 too. Solve Eq. (2) and Eqs. 3 and 4 first.

Use lists, vectors, etc. to store values. It handles lists, vectors, etc. Then it returns. Count them, etc. 5 remain.

The draws are i.i.d. normal variables. The draws are i.i.d. We sample them.

Press Tab. Then press Etc. to continue. Add approx. Five is fine.
